{
  "_comment": "Single source of truth for the PrintShield font shield. Run `python scripts/generate_font_shield.py` after editing. allow = fonts that ship with the OS. common_extras = fonts most users of that OS ALSO have (on Windows: the Microsoft Office font pack). The visible 'profile' is allow + common_extras: profile fonts the user lacks are emulated, and every font on the block list outside the profile is hidden. Measured with amiunique.org, a Windows-defaults-only list scored 0.00% while the Windows + Office list scored 1.21%, so matching the common profile beats showing the smallest possible list. The Windows extras list contains only the Office fonts that a real Office install exposes as their own family in Chrome (verified on a real Office machine); style-named faces such as 'Eras Bold ITC' are not detectable there, so they are hidden too. Windows 'allow' includes fonts bundled in the same file as a default font (MS PGothic and MS UI Gothic with MS Gothic, NSimSun with SimSun) and the Windows 11 Cascadia fonts: hiding any of them made the list unique.",
